    "reason": "[ev-4e83bbc5b12c] gives the background: since #18388, ApplicationSet Git generators only work with repo credentials that have no AppProject set, which causes hard-to-diagnose errors. That points to Git generators using project-scoped credentials as the exposed case. But the resolution steps in [ev-0dfc5b50bfff] are struck through (an abandoned approach), and the excerpt is cut off before the approach that was actually merged. The changelog line [ev-99d47f7e30ee] only says the fallback was \"improved\". The changed files [ev-fea272151d74] touch the controller's command file and the Git generator and projects docs, which suggests a new option or documented behaviour, but the evidence doesn't say what the new fallback does or whether it must be turned on. So the consequence for an operator who does nothing (and the exact exposure) can't be written; the final PR description, or the diff of those docs and the controller flags, is needed.",
